# `nestjs/no-redundant-wiring-test`

First apply the ESLint autofix for `nestjs/no-redundant-wiring-test`. If violations remain, follow [fix-nestjs-redundant-wiring-test](.cursor/skills/fix-nestjs-redundant-wiring-test/SKILL.md).

The rule reports a test whose body is only `expect(value).toBeDefined()` when its suite, the outermost `describe`, already contains another executable test. The title is ignored.

**Remember:** the autofix removes that test statement and nothing else. A remaining violation means removal would change surrounding syntax, or a comment might belong to something else. Judge that leftover. Do not replay the fixer by hand.

**Do not:** disable the rule, copy the wiring assertions into another test, add a test so this one can be deleted, or remove setup, mocks, or bindings because they now look unused.

**Do:** let the autofix delete every wiring test it can remove safely. For a violation it leaves, remove only that test, and keep the comment or surrounding syntax the fixer would not take.
